## What the two checkboxes do
A save writes the ENTRY CONFIG -> the loader validates it against THIS schema at the next boot ->
the panel registration reads it. So the checkbox decides the NEXT BOOT's pages, which is exactly what
the mpd settings bridge already declares for this namespace (`applies: "restart"`). It STICKS because a
page whose checkbox is OFF is never registered, and nothing re-adds a panel that was never registered.

## Bounds (named, not implied)
- NOT live: flipping + saving applies at the next dsh boot; a live flip needs runtime reconciliation
  (dispose + re-register on a settings-document update).
- The dialog lists the row's knobs by their schema key names (`panel`, `workmate`); no bilingual label
  table was added for another row's config keys.
